## 9) Regular Expressions and Text Parsing

```python
import re

log_pattern = re.compile(
    r"^(?P<timestamp>\S+\s+\S+)\s+(?P<level>INFO|WARN|ERROR)\s+(?P<message>.*)$"
)

match = log_pattern.match(line)
if match and match.group("level") == "ERROR":
    print(match.group("message"))
```

### Regex guidance
- Compile patterns reused in a loop.
- Use named groups for readable parsing.
- Prefer simple string methods when regex is unnecessary.
- Be careful with greedy patterns and catastrophic backtracking.
- Never use regex alone as a complete security validator for complex formats such as URLs or email addresses.

