## 12) Logging and Configuration

Use `logging` instead of scattered `print` statements for operational scripts.

```python
import logging

logging.basicConfig(
    level=logging.INFO,
    format="%(asctime)s %(levelname)s %(message)s",
)
logger = logging.getLogger(__name__)
logger.info("Starting import")
logger.warning("Skipped %d invalid rows", invalid_count)
```

Configuration priority commonly follows: command-line argument, environment variable, configuration file, safe default.

```python
import os

api_url = os.environ.get("API_URL", "https://example.invalid/api")
api_token = os.environ["API_TOKEN"]
```

Never commit secrets or print authorization headers.

