## 18) Security Checklist

- Keep secrets in environment variables or a secret manager.
- Validate and normalize user input.
- Use allowlists for file extensions and commands.
- Prevent path traversal with resolved paths and an allowed root directory.
- Avoid `eval`, `exec`, and unsafe deserialization of untrusted data.
- Use parameterized SQL queries.
- Use HTTPS and certificate validation for network calls.
- Apply least-privilege permissions.
- Avoid logging passwords, tokens, and sensitive payloads.
- Set timeouts on network and subprocess operations.
- Review dependencies and pin versions where appropriate.

